From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t20: forward private ioctls from the frame channel to the core

The vendor libimp issues VIDIOC_ISP_PRIVATE_IOCTL on the frame channel
for the frame-source commands.  frame_channel_vidioc_default() only
knew the VIDIOC_DEFAULT_CMD_* shorthand and returned -ISP_ERROR for the
multiplexer, so the libimp closed the device and retried.

Forward the multiplexer to the parent video-in subdev, which now passes
it on to the ISP core.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-frame-channel.c
+++ b/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-frame-channel.c
@@ -817,6 +817,11 @@
 		case VIDIOC_DEFAULT_CMD_LISTEN_BUF:
 			ret = frame_channel_listen_buffer(vdev, arg);
 			break;
+		case VIDIOC_ISP_PRIVATE_IOCTL:
+			/* Frame-source commands live in the ISP core. */
+			ret = v4l2_subdev_call(vdev->parent, core, ioctl,
+					       cmd, arg);
+			break;
 		default:
 			ret = -ISP_ERROR;
 			break;
